  "_instructions": "Source of truth for the build. DO NOT delete, edit, or renumber existing ids/titles. Statuses: passing (done+proven), failing (actionable), deferred (postponed; notes say when actionable; notes starting \"Needs a human:\" = waiting on a human, and features depending on it are held; \"Needs a human: verify\" = built and green, only a human check left, and an unattended run builds its dependents), superseded (dead, kept for history), review (built, awaiting the independent evaluator; never picked as next). Flip failing->passing only when a test or the stated manual check proves it. Append new features with the next id in their milestone. Work ONE feature per session: lowest milestone, then lowest id, among 'failing'. Record on every feature: depends_on (ids whose code it cannot build or test without; order alone is not a dependency) and paths (the files it changes, or the narrowest folder it owns; name shared files explicitly) let an orchestrated run build independent features in parallel; omit either and the feature runs sequentially. Optional top-level shared_paths (files many features add lines to; absent = README.md and CHANGELOG.md, [] = none: they never keep lanes apart, a merge conflict only in them keeps both sides) and max_lanes (default 5). Optional exclusive (string): features sharing a resource (simulator, device, database) give it the same name and are never built in the same parallel batch. Optional evaluator opt-in: evaluate (\"ui\" = an independent evaluator must pass it before it becomes passing; absent or \"none\" = no evaluation), bar (concrete reference to judge against), eval_attempts (integer, orchestrator-owned). Optional effort: effort (low|medium|high|max) = how much verification and edge-case testing the feature deserves beyond its verify check; absent = the CLI's default effort. Required model size: model (small|medium|large, or a CLI's own alias) = which size of model builds the feature, apart from effort; every failing, review or deferred feature must carry it (harness-audit fails without it). Optional second opinion: second_opinion (claude|codex|copilot) = that CLI's agent re-judges the feature read-only after the builder, like evaluate it ends the session in review.",
